# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.

card end_contact
type ending
cat ending
when flag signal_contact
when res food >= 1
text Old Friend. Their hail reached Cargo 2 between boots, years late and just in time. The blinking stops. On the next pass it answers, in a format nobody has used in years. Anyone could have answered. One tap was enough.

card end_followed
type ending
cat ending
when flag echo_heard
text Company. Seven ships set down beside Cargo 2. Its lights are still blinking every eleven seconds, the way they did the whole time nobody answered. It can wait a little longer. Somebody gets to knock.

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
when flag arrive_wait
text Patience. The fleet waits out the storm in a long orbit. Every night, through the dust, one point of light keeps time at the edge of the landing zone. When the sky clears, seven ships go down to meet it.

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
when flag arrive_hold
text Through the Dust. The fleet holds the plan and goes down into the storm, radar full of sand. Out of the brown, every eleven seconds, a light. Seven ships land on it.

card end_long_way
type ending
cat ending
text The Long Way Round. Seven ships, one planet. After landing, they walk to Cargo 2 in their suits and open the hold. The first crate has Sharpie on it, in a hand they know: "You'll thank me." Everyone does.
